\section{Minerva Noctua: EMA-ACR + SFT Distillation (Flush Buffer)}

This document describes the EMA-ACR + SFT distillation variant used by:
\texttt{train\_minerva\_noctua\_llama3b.sh},
\texttt{train\_minerva\_noctua\_llama8b\_lr0.05\_textcnn\_mlh\_t0.7\_p0.9\_defer\_ema.sh},
and \texttt{train\_minerva\_noctua\_qwen4b.sh}. These wrappers invoke the same
core script and only change the base model path.

\subsection*{Notation}
Let the training set be $\mathcal{D}=\{(x_i,y_i^\*)\}$, where $x_i$ is the
original Minerva prompt and $y_i^\*$ is the ground-truth label (ID, set of IDs,
or vector depending on the task). The actor policy is $\pi_{\theta}$ and the
EMA teacher is $\pi_{\phi}$. Rewards are computed by the Minerva verifier
$R_{\text{minerva}}(\cdot)$, returning $r_{\text{base}}\in[0,1]$.

\subsection*{Step 1: RLVR Rollouts and GRPO Update}
For each batch $\mathcal{B}_t$, generate $N=8$ rollouts:
\[
y_{i,j}^{\text{rlvr}} \sim \pi_{\theta_t}(\cdot \mid x_i), \quad j=1,\dots,N.
\]
Score each rollout with the verifier:
\[
r_{i,j}^{\text{base}} = R_{\text{minerva}}(x_i, y_{i,j}^{\text{rlvr}}, y_i^\*).
\]
Update the actor with GRPO on the RLVR rollouts (standard RLVR objective).

\subsection*{Step 2: Hard-Example Gating}
Compute the per-UID maximum reward:
\[
m_i = \max_{j} r_{i,j}^{\text{base}}.
\]
Only ``hard'' UIDs are eligible for ACR:
\[
\mathcal{H}_t = \{i \mid m_i < 1.0\}.
\]
CVSS tasks are excluded from ACR regardless of $m_i$.

\subsection*{Step 3: ACR Prompt Construction}
For each $i\in\mathcal{H}_t$, build an answer-conditioned prompt by appending
an ACR block to the last user message:
\[
x_i^{\text{acr}} = x_i \oplus b(y_i^\*, d_i),
\]
where $d_i$ is the canonical label-details text (if available). If the prompt
exceeds the ACR length limit, details are truncated; if still too long, the
details are omitted; otherwise the sample is skipped.

\subsection*{Step 4: Deferred ACR Generation with EMA Teacher}
Prompts $x_i^{\text{acr}}$ are buffered each step and only generated on the
distill interval $I=10$. At those steps:
\[
y_{i,k}^{\text{acr}} \sim \pi_{\phi_t}(\cdot \mid x_i^{\text{acr}}), \quad k=1,\dots,K,
\]
with $K=4$, temperature $\tau=0.7$, and nucleus sampling $p=0.9$.
The EMA teacher is initialized by copying the actor parameters and is updated
after every actor update:
\[
\phi_t = \alpha \phi_{t-1} + (1-\alpha)\theta_t, \quad \alpha=0.995.
\]
Non-parameter buffers (e.g., normalization statistics) are copied directly:
\[
b^{\phi}_t \leftarrow b^{\theta}_t.
\]
The EMA model is inference-only (no gradients) and is used only for ACR
generation; RLVR rollouts always use $\pi_{\theta}$. If EMA is disabled or
unavailable, ACR generation falls back to the actor weights.
ACR rollouts are generation-only (no PPO update on these samples).

\subsection*{Step 5: ACR Reward and Filtering}
Each ACR rollout is scored with the verifier to obtain $r_{i,k}^{\text{base}}$,
then converted to an ACR score:
\[
r_{i,k}^{\text{acr}} = r_{\text{correct}} \cdot r_{i,k}^{\text{base}}
 - \lambda \cdot \mathbb{1}[\text{leak}],
\]
with $r_{\text{correct}}=0.1$ and $\lambda=0.5$. A rollout is eligible if:
\[
r_{i,k}^{\text{base}} \ge \tau_{\text{base}} \;\wedge\;
f_{\text{heur}}(y_{i,k}^{\text{acr}})=1 \;\wedge\;
s_{i,k} \ge \eta,
\]
where $\tau_{\text{base}}=1.0$, $f_{\text{heur}}$ enforces
minimum reasoning length (100 chars), minimum overlap Jaccard (0.05),
and degenerate n-gram checks (rep-3 $\le 0.70$, rep-4 $\le 0.75$), and
$s_{i,k}$ is the ML leak score from a TextCNN classifier with threshold
$\eta=0.5$.

\subsection*{Step 6: ML-Based Per-UID Selection}
When ML filtering is enabled, selection is based on the ML score:
\[
k^\* = \arg\max_{k \in \mathcal{E}_i} s_{i,k},
\]
with uniform random tie-break among the top-scoring candidates. The selected
pair is $(x_i, y_{i,k^\*}^{\text{acr}})$, where the input is the original
prompt (no hints).

\subsection*{Step 7: SFT Distillation (Flush Buffer)}
Selected pairs are appended to a distill buffer $\mathcal{Q}$. At each distill
interval, sample up to $M=256$ pairs and perform one SFT update:
\[
\mathcal{L}_{\text{sft}} = -\sum_{(x,y)\in\mathcal{S}} \sum_t
\log \pi_{\theta}(y_t \mid x).
\]
The distill update uses a scaled learning rate:
\[
\text{lr}_{\text{sft}} = \gamma \cdot \text{lr}_{\text{rlvr}}, \quad \gamma=0.05.
\]
The buffer is flushed after each distillation step (\texttt{buffer\_mode=flush}).

\subsection*{Hyperparameters (Noctua EMA-SFT)}

\textbf{Data and model}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
Base model & Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, or Qwen3-4B-Base \\
Train data & \texttt{rlvr/mydata/minerva\_base/minerva\_base\_train.parquet} \\
Val data & Minerva dev + Athena CTI parquets + \texttt{seceval\_mini} \\
Label details & \texttt{dataset/label\_details} \\
\end{tabular}

\textbf{RLVR baseline (GRPO)}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
Advantage estimator & \texttt{grpo} \\
RLVR rollouts per prompt & 8 \\
Rollout backend & \texttt{vllm} \\
Max prompt length & 2048 \\
Max response length & 1024 \\
Actor LR & $1\times10^{-6}$ \\
\end{tabular}

\textbf{ACR prompt and gating}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
ACR max prompt length & 4096 \\
ACR max details chars & 8096 \\
Hard gating & max reward $<1.0$ \\
Skip CVSS tasks & true \\
\end{tabular}

\textbf{ACR generation (EMA)}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
ACR rollouts per prompt & 4 \\
Temperature / top-p & 0.7 / 0.9 \\
Deferred generation & true \\
EMA alpha & 0.995 \\
\end{tabular}

\textbf{ACR reward and filtering}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
$r_{\text{correct}}$, $\lambda$ & 0.1, 0.5 \\
Min reasoning chars & 100 \\
Min overlap Jaccard & 0.05 \\
Degenerate rep-3 / rep-4 & 0.70 / 0.75 \\
ML filter & TextCNN response-only, threshold 0.5 \\
\end{tabular}

\textbf{SFT distillation}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
Distill interval $I$ & 10 steps \\
Batch size $M$ & 256 \\
LR scale $\gamma$ & 0.05 \\
Buffer mode & flush \\
\end{tabular}
